# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in one provider option below, then
# restart `npm run dev`. Used to reconstruct explained courses from incomplete
# slides, create multidimensional cards, and provide optional tutoring.
# Existing content and tracked revisions do not require a model.

# --- Option A: Claude API (requires an API key from
# console.anthropic.com) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# --- Option B: Ollama (runs locally — needs Ollama
# installed and running: https://ollama.com, then `ollama pull qwen3.5:4b`) ---
# Run npm.cmd run ollama:setup on Windows, then restart the app and worker.
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
# OLLAMA_AUDIT_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
# OLLAMA_ACCURACY_MODEL=qwen3.5:4b
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=32768
# MORROW_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
# MORROW_GENERATION_CONCURRENCY=1
# MORROW_ACCURACY_CONCURRENCY=1

# If both are set, LLM_PROVIDER picks which one wins ("anthropic", "openai", or "ollama").
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama

# --- OpenAI API ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# Optional: audit generated content with a different model from the same provider.
# These calls use that provider's API credits. Defaults to the generation model.
# OPENAI_AUDIT_MODEL=your-audit-model
# ANTHROPIC_AUDIT_MODEL=your-audit-model
# OLLAMA_AUDIT_MODEL=your-installed-vision-model

# Optional adversarial factual reviewer, in addition to the primary audit.
# Defaults to the audit model, then the generation model. Using the same model
# is a separate review call, not evidence of independent scientific validation.
# OPENAI_ACCURACY_MODEL=your-accuracy-model
# ANTHROPIC_ACCURACY_MODEL=your-accuracy-model
# OLLAMA_ACCURACY_MODEL=your-installed-accuracy-model

# Slides -> explained course -> reviewed cards (up to four calls per batch).
# One production engine; historical pipeline flags no longer select an engine.
# Import reconstructs an explained lesson before generating its cards.
# Cloud: 3 concurrent batches, short first batch; local Ollama: 1. Range: 1–4.
# MORROW_GENERATION_CONCURRENCY=3
# Independent factual-review batches per section: default 2, range 1-3.
# With 3 sections this allows up to 6 simultaneous review calls. Use 1 if rate-limited.
# MORROW_ACCURACY_CONCURRENCY=2
# `npm start` runs the durable worker beside Next.js and restarts it on crash.
# `npm run dev` keeps inline generation unless worker mode is explicitly set.
# In development worker mode, also run `npm run worker`.
# MORROW_GENERATION_EXECUTION=worker
# Worker idle queue polling, bounded to 250–10000 ms. Default: 500 ms.
# MORROW_WORKER_POLL_MS=500
# If a reverse proxy changes the server URL, set the browser's exact origin.
# Cross-site browser mutations are rejected. This is not user authentication.
# MORROW_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://morrow.example.com
# Per-call timeout, 10–600 seconds. Default: cloud 60s, Ollama 300s.
# MORROW_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# Shared document budgets stop subsequent paid calls, retaining checked content.
# In-flight calls can exceed the token threshold by their actual responses.
# MORROW_GENERATION_MAX_REQUESTS=120
# MORROW_GENERATION_MAX_TOKENS=500000
# Optional hard output ceiling per model call, range 2048–16384.
# MORROW_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=8192
# Optional cost estimates, in USD per million tokens, for your configured models.
# For different generation/audit prices use a conservative blended rate.
# These estimates are not provider invoices and do not account for cache discounts.
# MORROW_INPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=1
# MORROW_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=4

# Recommended first: npm.cmd run evaluation:check, then the bounded pilot CLI.
# It chooses Sol/Sonnet explicitly and reserves a cumulative $2 pilot budget.
# No model calls occur without --live. See references/model-evaluation.md.
# Optional installation-wide persistent scheduling budget, across imports/chat.
# Failed calls retain their full reservation and halt the session for reconciliation.
# Native input token counting + margin + maximum output are reserved before sending.
# This local guard is not a guaranteed provider invoice ceiling.
# MORROW_LLM_MAX_USD=2
# MORROW_LLM_BUDGET_SESSION=installation
# MORROW_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
# For an OpenAI quality trial (Responses API is selected automatically):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
# OPENAI_AUDIT_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
# MORROW_INPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=2
# MORROW_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MILLION=10

# Optional: enable protected course-transfer APIs. At least 32 characters.
# Generate a separate random token for each installation; do not publish it.
# MORROW_TRANSFER_TOKEN=your-random-token-with-at-least-32-characters

# Optional local Tesseract executable for sparse/scanned PDF pages.
# OCR never certifies a scientific statement: generated content also uses
# the original image. Normal text PDFs do not invoke OCR.
# MORROW_OCR_BINARY=C:/Program Files/Tesseract-OCR/tesseract.exe
# MORROW_OCR_LANGUAGES=eng+fra

# Optional protected multi-user mode. Provision accounts before enabling.
# node scripts/users.mjs your-name --owner (password read from stdin)
# The owner keeps the existing local courses; other accounts are isolated.
# MORROW_AUTH=required
